WEBVTT

00:00.940 --> 00:04.030
At USJ and the training camp...

00:04.970 --> 00:06.880
I led them to us.

00:08.160 --> 00:10.950
Midoriya, I...

00:12.020 --> 00:13.920
am a terrible villain.

00:14.440 --> 00:16.110
That's not it, is it?

00:17.000 --> 00:20.120
Take my hand, Aoyama.

00:21.740 --> 00:26.420
Because you can still be a hero!

02:02.100 --> 02:05.790
The current situation is that Aoyama

02:05.790 --> 02:08.650
is the only one who may be
able to trick All For One!

02:14.010 --> 02:15.070
How?

02:17.970 --> 02:19.120
Why?

02:22.570 --> 02:24.990
Why would they do this for me...?

02:26.850 --> 02:28.870
Even though I'm a terrible villain...?

02:30.410 --> 02:33.060
Wait a minute, guys!

02:33.060 --> 02:34.500
You're moving too fast.

02:34.500 --> 02:36.200
A crime is a crime.

02:36.200 --> 02:38.840
I don't want to say it, but you know...

02:38.840 --> 02:41.000
you guys are the main victims here.

02:41.610 --> 02:44.010
Can you still trust him?

02:47.600 --> 02:50.870
That all happened in the past.

02:51.790 --> 02:54.730
We weren't able to understand his feelings,

02:54.730 --> 02:56.860
so it's partly our responsibility, as well.

02:57.280 --> 03:01.710
That's why we want to take
the hand of our classmate

03:02.580 --> 03:04.650
who is crying in despair as his friend.

03:05.240 --> 03:07.250
And for him to take our hands.

03:07.670 --> 03:11.030
Because that's the only way

03:11.880 --> 03:16.090
we can be equals again.

03:17.020 --> 03:20.280
I went through a lot at the
training camp, you know.

03:20.280 --> 03:23.120
I'll give you five blasts of my Howitzer.

03:23.120 --> 03:25.390
That's too hard to respond to, so stop it.

03:25.390 --> 03:26.770
Yeah!

03:26.770 --> 03:30.690
You went with what All For One said 'cause
you thought you couldn't beat him, right?

03:30.980 --> 03:32.870
But it's different now.

03:32.870 --> 03:35.510
You told your parents you
wanted to stop, right?

03:36.010 --> 03:37.760
When we went to go stop Midoriya,

03:38.270 --> 03:40.820
did anyone say anything bad
about being Quirkless?

03:41.270 --> 03:45.020
Did anyone hate the guy who was hiding
something while holding back tears?

03:45.800 --> 03:48.250
Back then, everyone said it, right?

03:48.550 --> 03:50.510
To let us share the responsibility, too!

03:50.510 --> 03:52.350
That we wouldn't let you go alone!

03:52.830 --> 03:56.330
That unnecessary meddling
was the essence of a hero!

03:56.330 --> 03:59.200
Aoyama, it's not over yet!

03:59.200 --> 04:01.890
Let's all get through this together!

04:01.890 --> 04:06.210
Aoyama! / Aoyama! / Aoyama!

04:06.210 --> 04:07.860
Wait a minute.

04:07.860 --> 04:10.140
Sorry to cut in right now,

04:10.140 --> 04:13.860
but first, we need to ask the Aoyamas
to cooperate with our investigation.

04:14.270 --> 04:17.030
All For One won't fall for any lies.

04:17.030 --> 04:20.360
You heard them earlier--If they
lie, they'll be punished.

04:20.670 --> 04:23.530
I understand how you feel, but
we need to calm down and--

04:24.060 --> 04:25.270
Midoriya.

04:26.280 --> 04:29.070
You said you would lead All For One
to where we wanted him, right?

04:30.150 --> 04:32.620
Did you have a concrete plan for that?

04:32.980 --> 04:35.340
No, not yet...

04:35.340 --> 04:37.660
That's what I thought. Jeez.

04:38.380 --> 04:39.700
Detective Tsukauchi,

04:39.700 --> 04:43.090
I bear responsibility for not catching
this as their homeroom teacher.

04:43.090 --> 04:46.420
However, I feel the same as the students.

04:46.420 --> 04:47.570
Aizawa!

04:48.230 --> 04:51.220
Aoyama, I still...

04:53.390 --> 04:56.030
have no intention of expelling you.

04:59.330 --> 05:02.600
As Class A's homeroom
teacher, I have an idea.

05:02.960 --> 05:04.290
An idea...?

05:04.830 --> 05:08.450
Detective Tsukauchi, can you make
arrangements so Aoyama and his parents

05:08.450 --> 05:11.010
cannot hear what I'm about to say?

05:11.010 --> 05:12.680
Yes, of course.

05:17.450 --> 05:19.950
The plan I came up with is...

05:23.480 --> 05:24.640
I see.

05:24.970 --> 05:27.550
Each location will need to be inspected...

05:27.940 --> 05:30.230
But it does seem like it could work!

05:30.520 --> 05:33.270
Yes, it all depends on him, though...

05:33.670 --> 05:36.160
We only have one week.

05:36.160 --> 05:37.560
Instead of just sitting and waiting...

05:38.440 --> 05:40.690
It could be worth trying, huh?

05:41.130 --> 05:44.230
I'll bring this back to HQ
to work out the details.

05:48.960 --> 05:53.950
Please refrain from discussing this with
anyone who was not present today.

05:55.080 --> 05:56.240
Aoyama!

06:13.720 --> 06:16.010
We should start getting ready.

06:16.010 --> 06:17.060
Yeah.

06:17.370 --> 06:20.110
First, I need to do something
about my costume.

06:20.110 --> 06:22.360
It's been worn to pieces.

06:22.360 --> 06:23.410
Mine, too.

06:23.710 --> 06:25.870
We need to continue the intense training

06:25.870 --> 06:28.280
and improve our Quirks as much as we can.

06:28.280 --> 06:29.190
Yeah.

06:29.950 --> 06:31.030
Everyone...

06:32.040 --> 06:33.830
Let's make sure we defeat them.

06:34.620 --> 06:35.720
Yeah!

06:40.120 --> 06:42.540
In order to prepare for the next battle

06:43.530 --> 06:45.530
and make sure I'm completely ready...

06:46.590 --> 06:49.270
There's a piece of equipment I need fixed.

06:52.390 --> 06:53.570
Déjà vu.

06:55.470 --> 06:56.920
Ouch...

06:57.910 --> 06:58.710
Ow...

06:59.570 --> 07:02.970
Oh my, it's been a while,
hasn't it, Midoriya!

07:07.360 --> 07:09.930
Oh dear, I'm sorry.

07:10.390 --> 07:12.820
Did you need something, you two?

07:13.130 --> 07:15.220
Danger Sense didn't react.

07:15.220 --> 07:16.870
I must be tired today!

07:16.870 --> 07:18.760
I mean, those were breasts!

07:18.760 --> 07:20.750
Anyway, Hatsume--

07:20.750 --> 07:24.840
We have come here today to ask
you to repair our costumes.

07:25.980 --> 07:29.420
Why don't you just ask the item
agency like you usually do?

07:30.330 --> 07:35.710
Well, right now the item agency--basically
any kind of business--has come to a halt.

07:35.710 --> 07:37.770
That's why we came to the support course...

07:37.770 --> 07:41.090
Oh, really? No wonder!

07:41.090 --> 07:41.980
Huh?

07:41.980 --> 07:42.960
Huh?

07:44.260 --> 07:50.230
Don't tell me Hatsume isn't aware of
anything that happened out there?

07:51.560 --> 07:52.960
Hatsume!

07:52.960 --> 07:56.120
Why do you always make
things explode like that?

07:56.720 --> 07:59.690
You two are here to get your
costumes repaired, right?

07:59.690 --> 08:00.720
Come in.

08:07.750 --> 08:09.920
It looks different in here...

08:10.340 --> 08:13.270
The principal's pet
project--the U.A. Barrier.

08:13.270 --> 08:16.110
I'm in charge of its development,

08:16.110 --> 08:18.380
and I'm also keeping it running.

08:18.760 --> 08:21.100
The whole support course is involved.

08:21.490 --> 08:23.320
Is that right?

08:25.330 --> 08:27.240
Mid-Gauntlets...

08:27.240 --> 08:30.100
They use the latest in compression
technology, right?

08:30.100 --> 08:33.550
They're prototypes from overseas,
so there's no stock anywhere.

08:33.550 --> 08:35.360
I'd like you to fix them for me.

08:36.910 --> 08:38.630
Are you in a hurry?

08:39.090 --> 08:39.960
Yeah.

08:40.460 --> 08:42.730
Can't do it then, sorry!

08:43.120 --> 08:46.530
With this amount of damage, I would
basically be remaking them from scratch,

08:46.530 --> 08:49.010
but I don't have any of the condenium
needed for the compression mechanism

08:49.010 --> 08:50.380
so it's impossible right now!

08:50.380 --> 08:51.050
I'm sorry!

08:51.050 --> 08:53.450
You're walking away at an impossible speed!

08:53.450 --> 08:55.410
Hatsume, what about my armor?

08:55.410 --> 08:57.100
I can't do it without the
specification documents!

08:57.100 --> 08:58.090
Short and to the point!

08:58.390 --> 09:00.730
Don't worry, we'll make it for you.

09:00.730 --> 09:02.310
We're in the same class as Hatsume.

09:02.310 --> 09:04.740
Thank you very much! I am in your debt!

09:04.740 --> 09:06.280
It's fine, it's fine.

09:06.580 --> 09:08.520
It's unexpected, though.

09:08.520 --> 09:13.950
I thought a machinery maniac like Hatsume
would definitely take this on herself.

09:14.960 --> 09:17.480
Hatsume, what are you making?

09:20.920 --> 09:22.810
They're flying? Wow.

09:23.420 --> 09:28.080
Hatsume's also involved in
powering up the U.A. Barrier.

09:28.080 --> 09:32.170
She just keeps coming up with new mechanisms
for when we need to evacuate.

09:32.470 --> 09:34.000
I've said it before,

09:34.000 --> 09:37.270
but her vitality and ideas
are completely unique.

09:38.150 --> 09:42.870
If you want to cool your legs, then
why don't you run with your arms?

09:43.530 --> 09:45.530
Even if it's a 100% now,

09:45.530 --> 09:48.200
the next minute, it could become 90%.

09:48.520 --> 09:50.720
Once I think up a baby, I have to raise it!

09:50.720 --> 09:52.330
It's what I always say!

09:52.330 --> 09:54.200
What she always says!

09:54.530 --> 09:55.980
I see...

09:55.980 --> 09:58.880
That's why she hasn't given a sidelong
glance at what's happening outside

09:58.880 --> 10:01.330
and is just immersed in
the inventing she loves.

10:01.820 --> 10:04.960
Hatsume really is amazing...

10:04.960 --> 10:07.300
You're soft, Midoriya!

10:07.300 --> 10:09.480
As soft as polyethylene.

10:09.480 --> 10:11.200
Sorry, I don't get it...

10:11.200 --> 10:15.430
I at least know that you
heroes are in a pinch!

10:16.450 --> 10:18.690
We can't fight.

10:18.690 --> 10:22.670
That's why we're trying different things

10:22.670 --> 10:24.540
to make sure you can protect
as many as possible.

10:25.960 --> 10:28.410
See? It's the same.

10:29.110 --> 10:33.160
Inventing is the support
course's "hero work"!

10:34.950 --> 10:35.990
Hatsume--

10:36.910 --> 10:38.950
It's impossible to make
something exactly the same.

10:39.310 --> 10:41.690
They're inferior to the Mid-Gauntlets,

10:41.690 --> 10:45.190
but if you're okay with my
babies, please use them.

10:45.190 --> 10:46.820
They've even got gloves?!

10:46.820 --> 10:49.700
Wow, did you make them with
your left hand just now?

10:50.590 --> 10:54.050
Iida, I couldn't accurately
replicate your armor,

10:54.050 --> 10:55.180
but if you'd like--

10:55.180 --> 10:56.920
All right! Thanks!

10:57.270 --> 10:59.100
We were just getting ready...

10:59.100 --> 11:00.750
...to take their measurements.

11:01.670 --> 11:04.250
Please tell this to the
others in the hero course--

11:05.430 --> 11:06.730
Let's win this!

11:07.560 --> 11:08.530
Yeah. / Yeah.

11:11.430 --> 11:14.190
Oh, that was fast, you two.

11:14.190 --> 11:16.070
We just finished getting read--

11:16.450 --> 11:18.160
Oh good, we made it.

11:18.160 --> 11:20.710
Wouldn't their faces usually
go back to normal right away?

11:22.020 --> 11:25.080
I've heard about what
happened with Class A.

11:25.080 --> 11:28.740
But we can't waste another day.

11:29.090 --> 11:33.010
Early detection of the Paranormal Liberation
Front and the League of Villains

11:33.010 --> 11:35.780
and getting rid of them in one clean
sweep is still the best plan!

11:36.520 --> 11:40.180
We can't abandon the quickest
path to a decisive victory!

11:40.180 --> 11:43.760
Hesitating and stopping in our tracks
is playing right into their hands!

11:44.870 --> 11:49.290
Aoyama... I wonder if
he'll take our hands...

11:50.160 --> 11:51.700
I believe in him.

11:52.490 --> 11:55.740
Aoyama will definitely come back to us.

11:57.250 --> 11:59.730
I hope it doesn't turn
into a curse, though.

12:01.180 --> 12:02.940
I think it'll be fine.

12:03.950 --> 12:05.560
I'm sure he's looked hard

12:07.390 --> 12:11.230
at what he wants to be more than anyone.

12:15.910 --> 12:17.790
Let's switch gears!

12:18.040 --> 12:20.520
Midoriya, Bakugo, and Todoroki--

12:20.520 --> 12:23.590
We'll build teams around
these three and spread out!

12:24.870 --> 12:27.950
U.A. High School hero course Class 1-A!

12:27.950 --> 12:29.910
Join the search!

12:33.140 --> 12:36.650
Kansai Region

12:33.930 --> 12:35.990
Meanwhile, around the same time...

12:36.900 --> 12:39.070
Output level 100...

12:39.070 --> 12:40.850
Nejire Flood!

12:46.420 --> 12:48.870
Suneater, was anyone injured?

12:49.220 --> 12:52.820
N-No... Nejire...

12:52.820 --> 12:54.760
Thank you! Thank you!

12:54.760 --> 12:56.990
The villains have starting throwing their
weight around in the countryside, too,

12:56.990 --> 12:58.250
so we rushed out here...

12:58.250 --> 13:01.380
Don't worry, you're safe now.

13:01.380 --> 13:03.350
We'll take you to Shiketsu High School.

13:03.350 --> 13:05.640
It's a stronghold that rivals U.A.!

13:05.640 --> 13:07.960
Thank you! Can you just
let us see your face...?

13:07.960 --> 13:11.020
No... don't... I can't...

13:11.670 --> 13:14.420
Of course, we want to protect the evacuees,

13:14.420 --> 13:16.900
but as people leave the cities,

13:16.900 --> 13:19.620
we're getting a lot less
intel about the villains...

13:20.030 --> 13:21.470
It's rough.

13:21.780 --> 13:23.890
Now that this has happened,

13:23.890 --> 13:26.710
we won't be able to launch
surprise attacks anymore.

13:26.710 --> 13:32.250
We'll have to do the opposite, and that
means both sides need to be infallible.

13:32.780 --> 13:36.110
The real all-out war is about to begin!

13:38.630 --> 13:41.000
Tenya Iida

13:42.630 --> 13:45.010
Shota Aizawa

13:45.010 --> 13:47.890
Central Hospital.

13:47.920 --> 13:51.380
In order to keep coordination with
this critical facility secret,

13:51.750 --> 13:56.190
a number of police stations have moved
operations to adjoining spaces.

13:56.560 --> 14:02.940
League of Villains
Paranormal Liberation Front Counterforce HQ

13:57.040 --> 13:58.500
For Plan B--

13:58.500 --> 14:02.150
I've summarized the important points we
need for our second decisive battle.

14:02.780 --> 14:06.520
Young Aoyama is currently
awaiting his test results.

14:06.960 --> 14:11.960
Because of Aoyama, our
movements are now limited.

14:12.320 --> 14:15.370
Everyone here has been deemed trustworthy
based on various circumstantial evidence

14:15.370 --> 14:18.370
and actions, so we are ready
to move forward with this.

14:19.120 --> 14:22.560
We'll have the main force of heroes,
including Endeavor and Jeanist,

14:22.560 --> 14:24.430
out in the field taking command.

14:24.700 --> 14:27.680
Since this is an urgent but secret meeting,

14:27.680 --> 14:31.000
we're playing it safe and keeping
this to a small group.

14:32.410 --> 14:35.570
I understand all that, but--

14:36.060 --> 14:40.800
Wild Wild Pussycats!

14:40.800 --> 14:43.900
It's sad Ryuko and the others
couldn't be here, meow.

14:43.900 --> 14:45.510
Sorry about that.

14:45.510 --> 14:47.660
We don't suspect them or anything.

14:47.980 --> 14:48.570
Meow.

14:48.570 --> 14:49.540
Meow.

14:50.580 --> 14:54.370
Shigaraki and the others are
using my Search for evil, meow.

14:54.370 --> 14:56.230
I'll do my best to help.

14:56.230 --> 14:59.060
Let me hear those "important
points" you were talking about.

15:04.600 --> 15:09.950
This is something we have to do
whether it's Plan A or Plan B.

15:11.940 --> 15:13.340
We have to split them up.

15:14.940 --> 15:18.160
Based on the data from the
fight with Star and Stripe,

15:18.160 --> 15:22.340
Tomura Shigaraki is currently much
more powerful than All For One.

15:23.120 --> 15:26.150
As for All For One,

15:26.150 --> 15:29.040
those of you who saw the battle at Camino
should already know how strong he is.

15:29.770 --> 15:32.750
Plus, in addition to their
contact using radiowaves,

15:32.750 --> 15:36.430
there's the shared consciousness they
showed us in the attack on Tartarus,

15:36.430 --> 15:38.710
but we don't know how much
they actually share yet.

15:39.580 --> 15:43.580
So if they come at us
together, we cannot win.

15:43.950 --> 15:48.330
Then why didn't they use that against Star?

15:48.330 --> 15:51.190
He was probably trying to
avoid her calling his name.

15:51.190 --> 15:56.590
Since with New Order's rules, saying "All
For One" would probably have worked.

15:57.920 --> 16:00.020
For this second decisive battle,

16:00.370 --> 16:04.060
we should keep them at least
ten kilometers apart.

16:04.060 --> 16:07.730
That's the minimum prerequisite
for us to win.

16:07.730 --> 16:12.320
Of course, the other side will be moving
their pieces so that doesn't happen.

16:12.650 --> 16:14.650
That's exactly right, Tsukauchi.

16:16.180 --> 16:19.450
The fearsome fire that spread
and burned everything up.

16:20.490 --> 16:24.250
The threat we clearly experienced at
the training camp and mountain villa.

16:25.500 --> 16:30.210
Just having Dabi in the vanguard
will stop us in our tracks.

16:30.210 --> 16:34.800
So then, in order to separate
All For One and Shigaraki,

16:34.800 --> 16:36.530
we have to separate Dabi--

16:36.530 --> 16:38.270
Not just Dabi.

16:38.760 --> 16:41.480
Right. Everyone.

16:45.250 --> 16:47.060
We need to separate the enemy's main forces

16:47.060 --> 16:48.510
and crush each and every one of them.

16:48.860 --> 16:52.980
In order to do that, we need
to lure out the enemy!

16:53.420 --> 16:56.770
Isn't that a little too optimistic?

16:56.770 --> 16:58.570
If we could do that, we wouldn't
be having a hard time.

16:58.850 --> 17:04.490
Yes. That's why, in order to achieve
these conditions, we need a plan.

17:05.570 --> 17:07.010
Aoyama, huh?

17:07.750 --> 17:09.710
He's still shaken...

17:10.230 --> 17:14.320
A boy born Quirkless, being
used his whole life...

17:14.710 --> 17:16.520
I feel bad for him,

17:16.520 --> 17:19.470
but we can't prioritize our
own feelings over the world.

17:19.470 --> 17:21.790
It doesn't change the fact
that he abandoned society.

17:22.260 --> 17:25.880
In my position, I need to be careful.

17:26.320 --> 17:28.930
I want to believe...

17:29.550 --> 17:31.400
in Young Aoyama.

17:32.360 --> 17:35.550
And, I will believe...

17:36.460 --> 17:40.360
in his homeroom teacher, Shota Aizawa.

17:41.700 --> 17:45.560
The results have come back, and
we didn't find anything abnormal.

17:45.560 --> 17:49.110
There was nothing wrong with his brain
waves or nervous system, either.

17:51.470 --> 17:54.700
So the Quirk that allowed him
to make Lady Nagant blow up

17:54.700 --> 17:58.700
must have been acquired after
All Might defeated him.

17:59.620 --> 18:06.090
Come to think of it, if he were able to
plant something to make traitors explode,

18:06.090 --> 18:09.900
then he wouldn't have needed to make
an example of anyone by killing them

18:09.900 --> 18:12.970
or give threats like "I'll
kill you if you lie to me."

18:13.880 --> 18:16.770
That's why All For One planted

18:18.100 --> 18:22.730
a seed of fear in this boy and his parents.

18:24.800 --> 18:25.960
Are you scared?

18:27.290 --> 18:32.450
You won't make many friends who'd
say all that in this lifetime.

18:33.240 --> 18:36.160
...we want to take the hand of our classmate

18:36.890 --> 18:39.010
who is crying in despair as his friend.

18:40.350 --> 18:42.170
What are you afraid of?

18:42.170 --> 18:44.070
All For One?

18:44.910 --> 18:45.730
Yes...

18:46.750 --> 18:49.090
And... I...

18:49.750 --> 18:51.700
can't twinkle like them...

18:53.270 --> 18:54.620
I'm scared of that, too.

18:56.270 --> 18:59.210
The more they believe in me,

19:00.140 --> 19:03.130
the less I can believe in myself.

19:04.910 --> 19:06.910
Even if I could take their hands,

19:07.780 --> 19:10.130
if All For One appears
in front of me again...

19:11.030 --> 19:13.960
I might do the same thing again.

19:14.760 --> 19:17.240
That's... what I'm scared of...

19:18.570 --> 19:20.440
That's why I want to give up...

19:21.340 --> 19:24.780
To go somewhere where there's no light...

19:25.480 --> 19:28.030
And wait for death...

19:29.200 --> 19:32.110
They would probably take extenuating
circumstances into consideration.

19:32.110 --> 19:34.600
But what you did won't go away.

19:35.630 --> 19:41.630
Aoyama, even when this fight is over,
you may not be able to stay at U.A.

19:42.570 --> 19:45.820
Those guys are your friends,
so they were nice about it,

19:45.820 --> 19:47.470
but I'm not like them.

19:47.470 --> 19:49.240
I'll give it to you straight.

19:49.930 --> 19:52.130
That fear planted inside him...

19:52.130 --> 19:54.170
I'll rip it out if I have to.

19:55.090 --> 19:56.650
Fight.

19:56.650 --> 19:59.640
All you can do now is fight.

20:00.040 --> 20:01.560
I know.

20:01.560 --> 20:03.970
I know that we have to win.

20:04.340 --> 20:07.650
I have to be a piece to help
us win... so I can be equal...

20:07.650 --> 20:09.780
I know this, but--

20:09.780 --> 20:10.900
That's true.

20:12.180 --> 20:18.540
And using you like this may make
us no different from All For One.

20:19.450 --> 20:23.510
But I won't let you give
up like this and die

20:23.510 --> 20:26.960
tormented by your actions.

20:28.640 --> 20:30.820
Not as long as I am your
hero course teacher,

20:31.260 --> 20:33.430
and you're my student.

20:34.510 --> 20:35.820
I still...

20:36.400 --> 20:38.930
have no intention of expelling you.

20:40.380 --> 20:46.000
I'm not going to teach any student to
live a life feeling indebted to others.

20:46.530 --> 20:48.670
Even if you're wretched and miserable,

20:48.670 --> 20:52.690
go walk with your friends who
held out their hands to you.

20:54.500 --> 20:55.980
We'll protect you.

20:56.770 --> 20:58.110
I can promise you this--

20:59.200 --> 21:03.000
If you're with them, you'll be fine.

21:07.720 --> 21:12.790
But, what can a lone criminal like me do?

21:13.990 --> 21:16.250
There's no way he's not scared.

21:16.250 --> 21:17.770
Anyone would be.

21:18.630 --> 21:19.570
That's why...

21:20.720 --> 21:23.650
We're not making you do this alone.

21:25.110 --> 21:30.600
You U.A. students, and us
teachers and pro heroes...

21:31.900 --> 21:33.510
That path...

21:33.940 --> 21:35.930
...is a path we'll all walk together.

21:36.020 --> 21:40.020
The Story of How We All Became Heroes

23:11.550 --> 23:15.750
Hey, come on! It's time to go.

23:17.630 --> 23:18.600
Okay.

23:20.000 --> 23:22.000
Preview

23:20.720 --> 23:22.010
Here's the preview!

23:22.490 --> 23:24.970
The final battle is approaching.

23:25.370 --> 23:26.890
Heroes, villains.

23:27.330 --> 23:31.400
All those preparing to fight are
dealing with various feelings.

23:32.060 --> 23:34.020
A past they don't want to remember.

23:34.020 --> 23:35.930
A now they want to change.

23:35.930 --> 23:38.950
And the future they should aim for.

23:39.560 --> 23:41.980
Next time, "Let You Down."

23:42.400 --> 23:46.580
What will we gain, and what will we lose?

23:45.980 --> 23:49.980
Next time

23:46.980 --> 23:48.290
Go beyond!

23:48.290 --> 23:49.720
Plus Ultra!
